Not that I disagree, in fact you are obviously right, but it can
awfully tedious to make a label for every single internal reference.
Also, only a fairly large tex can handle it.  I (and my coauthor)
had to remove quite a few labels (and expand some macros) in order
to get our book to compile under the limitation of 3500 CS names,
including labels.  We ended up with about 3495 such names.  This was less
than 3 years ago.  Nowadays, this is not serious, but it is still tedious.
Especially, say, if you have a problem with parts a,b,c,..., say and
you want to refer to b.  For then you have to have a different kind of
label and things can get quite complicated.

Michael Barr

